# 8p Game Translation Project

## Original English Strings (from Title.gd)

### Title Screen
- "EIGHT PAGES" (Title)
- "a forest · eight notes · one tall figure" (Subtitle)
- "BEGIN" (Start button)
- "HOW TO PLAY" (How to play button)
- "SETTINGS" (Settings button)
- "QUIT" (Quit button)
- "no escape recorded yet" (Best time when none)
- "best escape: %s   ·   %d/8 pages" (Best time format)
- "drag left to walk · drag right to look" (Touch controls text)
- "WASD move · SHIFT sprint · F light · E take · ESC pause" (Keyboard controls text)
- "a tribute to Slender: The Eight Pages" (Credit)

### How to Play Panel
- "HOW TO PLAY" (Header)
- "You are alone in a dark forest. Eight pages are pinned to landmarks: concrete walls, a tunnel, a silo, a truck, a shed, a ring of stones, a ruined bathroom and a watchtower.

Collect all eight, then get out.

He appears at the edge of the trees. Looking at him slows him down — but if you stare too long he will know, and he will run.

Static is his voice. When it rises, look away — or run." (Body text)
- "KEYBOARD:  WASD move · SHIFT sprint · F flashlight · E take page · ESC pause" (Keyboard keys)
- "TOUCH:  left side = virtual stick · right side = look · RUN to sprint · TAKE to pick up" (Touch keys)
- "BACK" (Back button)

### Settings Panel
- "SETTINGS" (Header)
- "MOUSE SENSITIVITY" (Slider label)
- "VOLUME" (Slider label)
- "INVERT LOOK Y" (Checkbox label)
- "FORCE TOUCH CONTROLS" (Checkbox label)
- "BACK" (Back button)

## Original English Strings (from HUD.gd)

### HUD Elements
- "PAGES" (Pages counter label)
- "0 / 8" (Pages counter format)
- "BREATH" (Stamina label)
- "FIND THE EIGHT PAGES" (Objective)
- "LEFT STICK — MOVE     RIGHT SIDE — LOOK     HOLD RUN TO SPRINT" (Touch hint)
- "ROTATE YOUR DEVICE  ·  BEST IN LANDSCAPE" (Rotate hint)
- "II" (Pause button)

### Pause Menu
- "PAUSED" (Header)
- "RESUME" (Resume button)
- "RESTART RUN" (Restart button)
- "TOUCH CONTROLS: AUTO" (Touch toggle button - changes to ON/OFF)
- "QUIT TO TITLE" (Quit button)

### End Screens
#### Win Screen
- "THE PAGES ARE YOURS" (Win title)
- "Eight pages. The forest lets you go.\nFor now." (Win subtitle)
- "PAGES  %d / 8        TIME  %s%s" (Stats format with optional BEST line)
- "BEST: %s" (Best time line)

#### Lose Screen
- "HE FOUND YOU" (Lose title)
- "You cannot outrun him. You can only refuse to look." (Lose subtitle)
- "PAGES  %d / 8        TIME  %s%s" (Stats format with optional BEST line)
- "BEST: %s" (Best time line)

### End Buttons
- "TRY AGAIN" (Retry button)
- "TITLE SCREEN" (Menu button)

## Translation Targets

### Russian (ru)
- Language: Russian
- Script: Cyrillic
- Considerations:
  - Gendered nouns and adjectives
  - Formal vs informal (informal preferred for games)
  - Line breaks should be preserved
  - Font compatibility (DejaVu supports Cyrillic)

### Chinese (zh-CN)
- Language: Simplified Chinese
- Script: Hanzi
- Considerations:
  - Character count reduction (Chinese is more compact)
  - Line breaks should be preserved
  - Font compatibility (DejaVu supports Chinese)

## Implementation Plan

1. Create translation files (JSON or CSV format)
2. Modify Title.gd and HUD.gd to use translation system
3. Add language selection in Settings
4. Test both translations

